<description>&lt;p&gt;Boko Haram is rebuilding its ranks by training about 8,000 new fighters, while women farmers in Gella have resisted the group to rebuild a community. Ambazonian separatists continue to target civilians, exemplified by the shooting of a journalist in Bamenda and ongoing attacks in the Anglophone regions. Cameroon is expanding security measures, deploying drones, joint border patrols, and the BIR rapid intervention force around Lake Chad, and has offered the Zina and Makary oil blocks to investors after a twelve-year halt. Online fraud is increasingly linked to human trafficking in Cameroon. The conflict caused 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixgFBVV95cUxQU1l5WXBqS0JMNU5uZEFZY2s1UURDQ2N2bDhwSnQxUnlUUjNYVEZQclR6NWh6Sk9yajVUN1JnMHYzYUhNWkxsU01kTm1FSW5NY25keWl2SE00Q2VaWlF6cy1RR3RmS3JNSFVZSVJtX3JBcVFRX1BXUGZ2TG5KTHFhVU5LNVBGcFVVbXNFMUNNek94dDRjUHEweFIteGNYaXJMVWJXOWZfU19zOWR4NHQ4LTRnUnFMd3VsOUxEZ2xtdTAtc3ktYVE?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxNX0Q3VGx6a0NIN210OTNKZVd6SndCOEhIelcteWZ1TTVfZTQzbGtCbVo5NkhuV3JUVmVJZkZSOEFjVDZISTZ1ZkVVdGQ3UVVzaVVkZlhyRVA5ZFNYNjVFUWN2Rzg0TUVicDhGLTlVMFFSelpDam1TdEE3cHhoNXBNc3hOMUtXT0tHM2dDRnNscUhIcktoQWRtSlIzWWpnVlRqR1VvMG1R?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxNOHpzSlRaOGdmMTZFd3hsRURVRnJUMHhfOF9HWEUyTFFMaEVMMG9QMS1SRklPamxwelBjRTdMeFlBY2FtYmVWYzNCRmpZM0RjV016MXZXQTZ6cVhJclhRYXFScVJXOFp3dndLRFRIdjEtS2xpci1yQjNrZXlmOGRCdnVVVHRZRW1HWkZPR0dwMUFIQzk4TEk1Q2ctNFdHQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Cameroon-Tribune&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Africa Intelligence&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBM